  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#4783\", \"PowerToys#16031\", \"PowerToys#39287\"], \"answer\": \"This feature request has been filed before: a hotkey to turn the monitor off immediately without sleeping or locking the PC. PowerToys has no such shortcut yet. Past tickets point to the umbrella ticket PowerToys#1052 (Quick Display adjustment, which lists \\\"sleep monitors\\\"), where it is tracked. You can add your scenario there or upvote the existing requests. Until then, use a workaround. (1) Make a shortcut or AutoHotkey script that sends the monitor-off message: `powershell (Add-Type '[DllImport(\\\"user32.dll\\\")]public static extern int PostMessage(int hWnd, int hMsg, int wParam, int lParam);' -Name a -Pas)::PostMessage(-1,0x0112,0xF170,2)`. Then assign a keyboard shortcut to it. (2) Run `nircmd.exe monitor off` through AutoHotkey. (3) Use Twinkle Tray, which can turn monitors off with a hotkey. In all of these, moving the mouse or pressing a key wakes the display, and the PC stays running, so your render continues. Note that Win+Pause is already a Windows system shortcut, so you may want a different key combination. One caveat from the tickets: after waking, some setups ask you to sign in again, depending on your sign-in settings. PowerToys Awake does not turn the screen off on demand. It only keeps the PC or screen awake.\"}",
